    "spans": [
     {
      "end": 651,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "Brown Fat and Browning for the Treatment of Obesity and Related Metabolic Disorders\nThe inducible brown adipocyte, beige adipocyte evolving by thermogenic activation of white adipose tissue have different origin and molecular signature from classical brown adipocytes but share the characteristics of high mitochondria content, UCP1 expression and thermogenic capacity when activated. Increasing browning may also be an efficient way to increase whole brown fat activity. Recent human studies have shown possibilities that findings in mice can be reproduced in human, making brown fat a good candidate organ to treat obesity and its related disorders."
     }
    ],
